CommitDate: Mon Aug 10 15:38:05 2026 -0500

    codefence: require BOTH code-root packages by SLOT (fail closed on empty/partial resolve)
    
    Follow-up to the PR #34 certification: #34 closed only the EMPTY PROTECTED_ROOTS case, but a PARTIAL
    resolve (one package's __file__ unresolvable) left a non-empty tuple that silently fenced only one
    package. disjoint_from_code now fails CLOSED unless BOTH expected packages resolve.
    
    Completeness is tracked by SLOT (which imported module resolved — collaborator from __file__,
    salienceos from salienceos.__file__), NOT by directory basename, so a package that legitimately
    lives in an odd-named dir (a case-insensitive checkout naming it SalienceOS, a symlink, an
    editable/vendor install) does NOT false-fail. This was the unanimous 5/5 fix from the completeness
    certification panel (which also over-rated a "decoy dir" fail-open that is unreachable — roots come
    only from imported modules, never a filesystem scan; grok/qwen refuted it, confirmed against code).
    
    Subsumes gemini's names_code_root concern: completeness is enforced at Session construction, so no
    Session with incomplete roots exists, so no govern/approve path consults incomplete roots.
    
    Tests: incomplete-slots (empty / collaborator-only / salienceos-only) all fail closed; odd-basename
    + complete-slots does NOT false-fail. Suite 538, 3 skipped, green.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rpuvh681reoP8Xf53NfcGU

